# Signal Rust Engine Rules (`engine/**`, `benchmarks/**`)

Deep reference: `docs/engineering/RUST_ENGINEERING_GUIDE.md` | Skills: `signal-rust-crate-architect`, `signal-rust-physics-and-geometry`, `signal-universal-parts-registry`, `signal-cad-cam-plm-ops`.

## 1. Crate Structure & Token Efficiency
- Rust **2024 Edition**; every crate `lib.rs` declares `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` (audited SIMD/FFI leaves live in tiny micro-crates with `// SAFETY:` proofs + Miri + fuzz tests).
- Keep files `<= 300 LOC` (split `> 350 LOC`) with a 3-line `//!` header (`Module`, `Invariants`, `Spec`). Separate `types.rs`, `error.rs`, `stamping.rs`/`model.rs`, and `kernel.rs`; keep `lib.rs` to concise re-exports.
- Centralize ALL Protobuf/gRPC build-time codegen in `engine/crates/signal-proto` (`cargo-hakari` workspace-hack) — never add duplicate `prost`/`tonic` `build.rs` steps to domain crates.
- Respect strict acyclic crate layering: Tier 0 (`signal-core`, `signal-proto`) → Tier 1 (`signal-graph`, `signal-geom`, `signal-component`, `signal-parts`) → Tier 2 (`signal-lib-*`, `signal-module-sdk`) → Tier 3 (solvers, `signal-pcb`, `signal-ic`, `signal-mcad`, `signal-cam`, `signal-plm` & extended domain crates) → Tier 4 (`signal-render`, `signal-git-sync`, `signal-cell-wasm`, `signal-pod`, `signal-operator`).

## 2. Safety, Security & Error Handling
- Zero `.unwrap()`, `.expect()`, or unchecked `[i]` indexing on untrusted, network, Git, CAD-import, or parser inputs.
- Library crates use `thiserror::Error` with explicit typed variants; never expose `anyhow::Error` in library crate APIs.
- Wrap every DEK, token, PDK buffer, and confidential net name in `secrecy::SecretBox<T>` + `zeroize::ZeroizeOnDrop`; never log secrets into `tracing` fields.
- Never link LLVM or `dlopen` vendor `.so`/`.dll` inside `signal-pod` (use AOT Cranelift/`WASM-SIMD` build workers + out-of-process child `Firecracker`/`gVisor` IPC sandboxes for binary `IBIS-AMI`/`OSDI`).
- Never block `tokio` threads with CPU physics/crypto/DRC work, and never hold a `Mutex`/`RwLock` across `.await`.

## 3. Deterministic EDA Physics & Exact Geometry
- Use `#[repr(transparent)]` SI-unit newtypes (`Nanometers(i64)`, `Picoseconds(i64)`, `MicroVolts(i64)`, `NanoAmps(i64)`). Never mix raw `i64`/`f64` units in public APIs.
- `signal-geom`: store compact `i64` nm; ALWAYS promote cross-products/determinants to exact `i128` or Shewchuk adaptive predicates; preserve native Arc/Bézier/Euler curves.
- `0.5-ULP` cross-ISA determinism (`ARM64 Mac == x86_64 Linux`): use `core_math`, disable FMA contraction where required, iterate canonically (`BTreeMap`/sorted CSR, never `HashMap` iteration order), deterministic `rayon` tree-reductions, and per-`SignalEntityId` `ChaCha20Rng`.
- MNA SPICE: stamp exact `q(v)`/`Φ(i)` charge/flux conservation, Ruiz equilibration + `f128` refinement, CPU `KLU`/`CKTSO` (`< 25k`) ↔ GPU `cuDSS` (`>= 25k`), and Filippov Saltation + `Revolve` $O(\log N_t)$ checkpointing for switching adjoints.

## 4. Verification Before Commit
Run `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p <crate>` (then `--workspace`), `cargo deny check`, `cargo vet`, and relevant `benchmarks/` regressions.

## 5. Dev Response & Anti-Hallucination
Reply in **2–3 sentences max** (`Issue -> Fix -> Observed check result`). Verify crate/symbol/Cargo.toml versions before referencing; never claim green without observed exit code `0`.
